<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hannezo, Prost & Joanny (2014) PNAS & Krajnc & Ziherl (2015) PRE 3D epithelial sheet morphology (squamous-to-cuboidal-to-columnar scaling & apico-basal buckling) — MorphoEval overall 93.3/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 (v2) evaluation of `2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py` (overall weighted score: 93.4/100, up from 56.4/100 in v1). The remediated script minimizes both the 3D incompressible single-cell energy E_cell(A) and the 2D continuum + substrate bending energy functional F[w] via L-BFGS-B across the full 5-regime (Gamma_l/Gamma_a, K_sub) phase diagram (flat squamous, flat cuboidal, flat columnar, buckled columnar folds, and spherical acini); reproduces the 12-tissue comparative scaling across Mus musculus and Drosophila melanogaster (aspect-ratio Pearson r = 1.0000, log-log exponent 0.9963 ± 0.0022; wavelength Pearson r = 0.9993, RMSE = 1.25 um); validates all 5 E-cadherin knockdown and apico-basal Myosin-II perturbation controls; and segments the SHA-256-locked CC0 histology specimen (`epithelial_sheet_buckling_specimen.jpg`, h0 = 59.66 px, d0 = 13.31 px, aspect ratio h0/d0 = 4.4833, fold wavelength lambda_c = 264.0 px, lambda_c/h0 = 4.4252). Overall 93.3/100 (faithfulness 93.1, reproducibility 93.8); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit e93f00e; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 92, Parameter expressivity 93, Morphometric validation 94, Source and data traceability 95, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 94. Output judged: docs/media/epithelial_buckling_3d_comparison.png: rendered output of 2016-hannezo-epithelial-buckling-3d.py at e93f00e, image/png, 799978 B, 2169×1442 px, artifact_sha256 48e806331be54d983f03105bfccdb6e42e173dfb732c824f84de22bb955b1b0a (sha256 48e806331be54d983f03105bfccdb6e42e173dfb732c824f84de22bb955b1b0a), spec_fingerprint eabe5855ceb1bf4a12fea7ec7b30902813b84c0440d83d21ca21bb917876b36c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: eabe5855ceb1bf4a12fea7ec7b30902813b84c0440d83d21ca21bb917876b36c; artifact_sha256: 48e806331be54d983f03105bfccdb6e42e173dfb732c824f84de22bb955b1b0a; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/epithelial_buckling_3d/epithelial_buckling_3d_reference.json=eef9f75ed38ce872..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_3d/epithelial_sheet_buckling_specimen.jpg=cd05cc85a7f49dd2..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_3d/paper_citations.bib=e4556865f1879134..., datasets/epithelial_buckling_3d/scout_manifest.json=99741cb299962b18...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-epithelial-buckling-3d-audit." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Extend the 2D continuum + vertex sheet solver to a full 3D polyhedral scutoid vertex mesh capturing apical-to-basal neighbor intercalations in high-curvature tubular bends." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.33e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

